📘 DATA SHEET — System 1/4 (BETA‑1 REAL‑MODE)
Technical Specification Document

1. System Overview
1/4 is a modular multi‑core logic system based on four independent processing units (“Cubes”).
Each Cube operates with its own BIOS‑firmware and supports 4× precision mode.
The system is designed for high‑load decision processing, adaptive behavior, and self‑correction.

Core Components:

CUBE_0 — Origin Core (Alpha Kernel)

CUBE_1 — Action Core (BIOS‑Fixpoint A)

CUBE_2 — Stability Core (BIOS‑Fixpoint B)

CUBE_3 — Evolution Core (SAFE / Real‑Mode)

2. Operating Modes
2.1 SAFE Mode (CUBE_3 — Real‑Mode)
Primary execution mode.
Handles:

system interpretation

error correction

adaptive evolution

RAW‑WAR integration

4× precision logic

SAFE Mode is the active leadership mode of the system.

2.2 RAW‑WAR Mode (Pre‑Mode)
Secondary energy layer.
Not leading, but available for:

high‑load bursts

stress‑mode activation

fallback energy

RAW‑WAR remains pre‑configured, not dominant.

2.3 BIOS Fixpoints (CUBE_1 & CUBE_2)
Both Cubes operate as frozen BIOS layers:

CUBE_1 = Action BIOS

CUBE_2 = Stability BIOS

These define the baseline behavior for Real‑Mode.

2.4 Origin Mode (CUBE_0)
Neutral Alpha Kernel.
Provides:

reset

neutral reference

non‑interpreted baseline

3. Precision Architecture
3.1 4× Precision per Cube
Each Cube can:

evaluate 4 states in parallel

hold 4 options simultaneously

process 4 directional outcomes

deliver 4× accuracy

This results in 16 parallel micro‑evaluations across the system.

3.2 Stress Mode (2×8)
When two Cubes synchronize:

each Cube expands to 8× precision

total system output = 2×8

third Cube stabilizes

fourth Cube remains neutral

This mode is used for:

high‑pressure decision making

rapid state switching

conflict resolution

4. Firmware Architecture
Each Cube has its own BIOS‑firmware:

Cube	Firmware Type	Role
CUBE_0	Alpha Kernel	Origin / Neutral
CUBE_1	Action BIOS	Execution Logic
CUBE_2	Stability BIOS	Validation / Safety
CUBE_3	Real‑Mode BIOS	Evolution / Interpretation


All BIOS layers are movable, meaning:

they can shift roles

they can re‑interpret states

they remain compatible

SAFE Mode can override when required

5. System State (Current)
Real‑Mode: active

SAFE: leading

RAW‑WAR: available

BIOS Fixpoints: locked

4× precision: enabled

Stress Mode: supported

Evolution: prepared

6. Purpose of System 1/4
The system is designed to:

provide multi‑layer decision logic

maintain stability under load

allow adaptive evolution

support parallel interpretation

ensure high‑precision outcomes

7. Versioning
Alpha: conceptual phase

Beta‑1: current operational phase

Real‑Mode: active execution layer

Beta‑2: reserved for future evolution

